# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values you have.
#
# WINDOWS GOTCHA: create .env with `Copy-Item .env.example .env`, not with
# `Set-Content`/`Out-File`. Windows PowerShell 5.1 writes a UTF-8 byte-order
# mark, and that BOM corrupts the FIRST line of the file -- the first key
# silently fails to load while every other key works. (This first line being a
# comment means a stray BOM would only damage the comment.)

# The Odds API - https://the-odds-api.com (free "Starter" tier, 500 credits/mo)
# Each pull costs markets x regions = 1 credit. Expected use ~47/month.
ODDS_API_KEY=

# Silver Bulletin (Substack) session cookie.
# Substack sign-in is a passwordless magic link, so there is no password to
# script. Copy a live session instead.
#
# MUST come from natesilver.net, NOT substack.com. Substack issues a separate
# session per custom domain; a substack.com cookie authenticates as anonymous
# against natesilver.net and looks exactly like an expired one.
#
# Recommended -- paste the whole Cookie header:
#   1. Open https://www.natesilver.net logged in
#   2. F12 -> Network tab -> reload
#   3. Click the top request (document, to www.natesilver.net)
#   4. Request Headers -> find the `cookie:` line
#   5. Copy everything AFTER "cookie: " and paste below, unquoted
#
# A bare `substack.sid` value also works, but the full header is safer if
# Substack ever requires a companion cookie.
#
# Check it worked: `npm run spike:silver` prints an AUTH line.
SUBSTACK_SID=

# Yahoo OAuth 2.0 - https://developer.yahoo.com/apps/
# Only needed for the Phase 6 league tracker; safe to leave blank for now.
YAHOO_CLIENT_ID=
YAHOO_CLIENT_SECRET=
YAHOO_REFRESH_TOKEN=
YAHOO_LEAGUE_ID=7029

DATABASE_URL=./data/survivor.db
SEASON=2026

# Anthropic API key - https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Powers the injury-report modal (click a matchup on the Scorecard). Claude
# runs a live web search per game, so each click costs tokens; results are
# cached for an hour per game. Leave blank to disable the feature -- the modal
# then says so rather than erroring.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Only needed if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is an ORGANISATION-level key rather than one
# created inside a workspace. An unscoped key must name a workspace on every
# request; a workspace-scoped key carries its own and this stays blank.
# Find it in the Console URL when viewing a workspace: .../workspaces/<id>
ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=
